      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm stuck on an iam issue. i'm trying to let a lambda function write logs to an s3 bucket but im just getting \"access denied\" errors even though i thought i added the policy right. can u check this json for me?\n\n{\n  \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n  \"Statement\": [\n    {\n      \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n      \"Action\": [\n        \"s3:PutObject\"\n      ],\n      \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:s3:::my-company-logs/*\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It looks like your policy is quite restrictive, allowing only the ability to put objects in a specific S3 bucket (`my-company-logs/*`). However, IAM policies for Lambda functions typically require more access, such as `s3:PutObjectAcl` and `s3:GetObject`, to log metadata. You may need to expand your policy or reference the execution role of the Lambda function. Consider adding `s3:PutObjectAcl` and `s3:GetObject` to your policy as well.",
